nd I wonder if you  have to look at Andrew Luck because you  know they they missed by a year that  that he was gonna be coming back  and you know shoulder surgery is an  inexact science and the fact that he was  coming back and Andrew Luck it took him  even longer made me wonder  I mean cam says he's Superman and I  thought well maybe he really is but I  also look at that hit that he took from  TJ watt in the Steelers game that's why  I don't know if if there is more damage  in there but just I've never heard an  athlete really tell you in full I don't  know what's going on but I've tried  everything and he was so despondent that  that's when I thought man you gotta shut  him down for his own good cuz he doesn't  even know what's wrong with him what did  you take from that press conference when  cam was talking about the shoulder yeah  you know Dan that was pretty remarkable  because like you I had never heard an  athlete open up that much about what was  going on or what the lack of knowledge  about what was going on and I thought it  was really important first of all it  seems like a little bit of a cry for  help without coming out and saying I  need help with this and I think that  that's really important because when you  when you see him without hope mentally  physically you're not getting answers  then then that's something that is a  huge concern and the team has to then  step up and make sure they're taking  care of their franchise quarterback and  so I think that that moving forward not  only are our answers needed but time is  needed as well I think that he needs to  be given the time that it takes for not  only him to come back and play healthily  but also to to kind of make sure he gets  his mind right and also you know you  have to consider too he's been throwing  around this pain I mean you kind of see  it on some of the heaves and and the  tosses he's been throwing around the  shoulder almost because it's been  causing him pain and so he needs to make